(2. Abstract) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Weeds reduce crop yield by competing with crops for water, nutrients, and sunlight.) Tj
T*
(Manual removal is) Tj
T*
(labor-intensive, while blanket herbicide spraying increases cost and environmental) Tj
T*
(impact. This experiment) Tj
T*
(develops a Random Forest classifier for weed detection using five agriculturally) Tj
T*
(relevant features:) Tj
T*
(GreenIndex, Texture, Moisture, Height, and NDVI. A synthetic, domain-inspired dataset of) Tj
T*
(1000 samples was) Tj
T*
(generated to simulate crop and weed patterns under controlled laboratory conditions. The) Tj
T*
(dataset was divided) Tj
T*
(using a stratified 80:20 train-test split, and the model was tuned using GridSearchCV) Tj
T*
(with 5-fold) Tj
T*
(StratifiedKFold cross-validation. The best model achieved a cross-validated F1-score of) Tj
T*
(0.929 and test-set) Tj
T*
(performance of 94.0% accuracy, 94.7% precision, 90.0% recall, and 92.3% F1-score. The) Tj
T*
(confusion matrix showed) Tj
T*
(strong classification performance with only a small number of weed samples missed.) Tj
T*
(Feature-importance analysis) Tj
T*
(identified NDVI as the strongest predictor, followed by GreenIndex and Height. The) Tj
T*
(results indicate that Random) Tj
T*
(Forest can serve as a reliable and interpretable baseline for weed detection and can) Tj
T*
(support future precision) Tj
T*
(agriculture systems based on real image or sensor data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Objective) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(To develop and evaluate a Random Forest classifier that distinguishes weeds from crops) Tj
T*
(using vegetation-related) Tj
T*
(and morphological features, with the aim of achieving high classification performance) Tj
T*
(and supporting future) Tj
T*
(precision agriculture applications.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Problem Statement) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Input: Five features extracted from crop-field sensing or imaging systems: GreenIndex,) Tj
T*
(Texture, Moisture, Height, and NDVI.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Output: A binary label WeedPresent, where 1 indicates weed and 0 indicates crop.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Context: Weeds compete with crops for nutrients, light, water, and space, reducing farm) Tj
T*
(productivity. An automated classifier can support site-specific weed management by) Tj
T*
(helping identify weed presence accurately and consistently.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Dataset Description) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The experiment uses a synthetic, domain-inspired dataset created specifically for this) Tj
T*
(laboratory study. Rather) Tj
T*
(than relabeling generic machine-learning features, the dataset was generated using) Tj
T*
(separate feature distributions) Tj
T*
