T*
(The following Python script was used to generate the dataset, train the model, evaluate) Tj
T*
(performance, and save the artifacts:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    """Submission-ready weed detection demo using Random Forest.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    This script is designed for academic submission when only a synthetic dataset) Tj
T*
(    is available. The synthetic data is generated to reflect agricultural feature) Tj
T*
(    names more honestly than renaming generic `make_classification` columns.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    What the script does:) Tj
T*
(    1. Generates a reproducible, domain-inspired synthetic dataset.) Tj
T*
(    2. Uses a stratified train/test split to preserve class balance.) Tj
T*
(    3. Tunes a Random Forest using 5-fold cross-validation on the training set.) Tj
T*
(    4. Evaluates the best model on a held-out test set.) Tj
T*
(    5. Saves the trained model and feature importance table.) Tj
T*
(    """) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    from __future__ import annotations) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    from pathlib import Path) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    import joblib) Tj
T*
(    import numpy as np) Tj
T*
(    import pandas as pd) Tj
T*
(    from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier) Tj
T*
(    from sklearn.metrics import \() Tj
T*
(        accuracy_score,) Tj
T*
(        classification_report,) Tj
T*
(        confusion_matrix,) Tj
T*
(        f1_score,) Tj
T*
(        precision_score,) Tj
T*
(        recall_score,) Tj
T*
(    \)) Tj
T*
(    from sklearn.model_selection import GridSearchCV, StratifiedKFold, train_test_split) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
